# OpenCode iOS: mobile layout and NewTerm rendering profile.
# Applies after 0001..0017 to upstream e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944.
# No iPhoneOS SDK or new native runtime required; existing signed renderer is reused.
# Design reference: pageton/tui-design-skill ec54092ea3a47fb3aafe3abc3363bc5e911d1a14.
# Phone viewports keep the same focused composer across resizes, compact the home
# screen and preserve error/status plugins. iOS defaults to reduced motion,
# a steady cursor, 20fps/coalesced frames, synchronized output and legacy keys.
# Explicit user cursor/animation settings win. Other runtime defaults are preserved.
# String(platform) comparisons accommodate this port's extra iOS Node platform
# without weakening upstream TypeScript's Platform union.
# Tests (from packages/tui): bun run typecheck:tsc; bun test --timeout 30000
# test/mobile-ui.test.tsx test/mobile-terminal.test.ts test/config-v2.test.tsx
# test/feature-plugins/home-footer.test.ts test/feature-plugins/prompt-footer.test.tsx.
# Real NewTerm visual acceptance is separate from native frame/SSH protocol tests.

